                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I've played this game for over 10,000 hours.\n\nAt this point, I'm not even sure if I'm qualified to review it anymore, because I feel like the game has been reviewing my life instead.\n\nDuring the time I've spent playing this game, I could've learned a few languages, started a career, put my life somewhat in order and maybe done something actually useful with my time.\n\nBut what did I do?\n\nI spent hundreds of hours grinding the same spot, used the money I made to enhance gear, watched it blow up and stared at my screen thinking, “Seriously? That one had to fail too?”\n\nAnd what did I do after that?\n\nWent right back to the same spot.\n\nAt some point, my account actually surpassed me. My character's gear is worth more than my real life financial situation.\n\nWhen I first started, I told myself, “I'll play for 2-3 hours and quit if I don't like it.\n\nI liked it.\n\nWay too much.\n\nThe first few months were great. You make a new class, explore the world, work on your gear, kill bosses. Then eventually you realize what the game is actually about:\n\nGrind  → make silver → enhance gear → gear explodes → go back to the grind .\n\nAfter a while, you're not even grinding anymore. You're working a shift.\n\n“I'll grind for 2 hours today.”\n\n3 hours later: “Just one more hour.”\n\n5 hours later: “Might as well, I'm already here.”\n\n7 hours later: “I'll go to bed early tomorrow.”\n\nThe next day:\n\n“Wait, how's that new class?”\n\nAnd you're back in the game.\n\nThe enhancement system is basically a psychological experiment.\n\nYou enhance an item and it goes through. You’re happy.\n\nYou try another one and it fails.\n\nIt's fine.\n\nYou try again. Fails again.\n\nOkay.\n\nOne more.\n\nFails again.\n\nAt that point you're not even questioning the item anymore. You're questioning your life choices.\n\nWhy did I do this?\n\nWhat else could I have spent that money on?\n\nWhy am I still in the exact same place in this game?\n\nThen five minutes later:\n\n“Let's try one more.”\n\nBut I have to give it credit. The combat system is still really good. That's probably one of Black Desert's biggest strengths. You actually feel like you're controlling your character instead of just clicking on things. After playing for a while, combat in other games starts to feel slow.\n\nAnd the graphics still look great. Sometimes I just stop and look at the scenery and think, “Damn, this game actually looks good.”\n\n30 seconds later I'm back at the same grind spot.\n\nLife skills are another trap entirely.\n\n“I'll stop grinding and just do some relaxing fishing.”\n\nThen you start researching fishing gear.\n\nYou need silver for gear. You need to grind for silver.\n\nAnd 10 minutes later you're grinding again.\n\nI genuinely don't remember how many times I've quit this game.\n\nEvery single time:\n\n“I'm actually done this time.”\n\nOne month later:\n\nI wonder what they added in the new update.\n\nLog in.\n\nLook around for a bit.\n\n“Let me just check this one thing.”\n\nThree hours gone.\n\nDoes Black Desert have bad sides?\n\nAbsolutely.\n\nQuite a few of them.\n\nSometimes the game makes even the simplest things way more complicated than they need to be. Trying to figure out some cooking or alchemy stuff feels like you need a damn degree. Then you realize you need a worker, a specific node, a specific item, and somehow you're watching a 20-minute guide just to figure out how to cook a fucking meal.\n\nBut somehow, you keep coming back.\n\nBecause somehow, it always pulls you back in\n\nAfter 10,000 hours, I'm still playing the game. So either they're doing something right,\n\nor I have a serious problem.\n\nHonestly, the second option seems more likely.\n\nIf you're thinking about starting this game, I only have one piece of advice:\n\nIf you have too much free time, get enough sleep, and still have a social life, go ahead and start playing.\n\nI didn't think about it.\n\nIs it a 10/10 game? No. \n\nWould i play it for 10,000 hours ?\n\nI already fucking did.",
